ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 DrivesList / ChargingCurve precedents)
  SpeedProfilePageModel.kt      framework-free: registration ids; SpeedProfileData.parse
                                (decodes the raw SI /analytics/speed-profile JSON —
                                avg_speed_mps / peak_speed_mps / optimal_speed_mps +
                                distribution[].speed_bucket/readings/avg_power_w);
                                speedProfileEfficiency (verbatim web getEfficiency —
                                energy-first, battery-delta fallback); drivesInRange (web
                                `drives` window useMemo); bucketEfficiencyMap + deriveSpeedProfile
                                (web bucketEfficiency + scatterData folds);
                                SpeedProfileDisplayPrefs (web useUnits); SpeedProfileRange
                                (web useRangeState, all-time default = 2015-01-01..today);
                                mapResource; recordSpeedProfilePageOpened (view.opened).
  SpeedProfilePageSource.kt     seam over DrivingRepository.speedProfile (web useSpeedProfile,
                                GET /analytics/speed-profile [start,end]) + drives (web useDrives)
                                + SettingsStore.settings + SelectedVehicleStore.
  SpeedProfilePageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; speedProfileState: StateFlow<UiState<
                                SpeedProfileData>> gated on the active vehicle (web
                                useSelectedVehicle) and re-collected on window/refresh; drives:
                                StateFlow<List<Drive>> enrichment feed; displayPrefs StateFlow;
                                setRange / refresh / retry / recordViewOpened.
  SpeedProfilePage.kt           stateful entry + stateless content; loading/empty/error/success;
                                the hero-gauge panel, the speed-distribution bar chart, the
                                per-bucket detail-card grid, the efficiency-vs-speed Compose-canvas
                                scatter + tier legend, the efficiency-insight callout, and the
                                DateRangeFilter range control.
  SpeedProfilePageHost.kt       SpeedProfileRoute + SpeedProfilePageHost.register() for the
                                `speedProfile` / `/speed-profile` destination (Destinations.kt L74;
                                registered in TeslaSyncApplication.kt).

DATA SOURCES (each bound through the ViewModel's StateFlow over the KMP core, P1/S8)
  useDrives        → DrivingRepository.drives(vehicleId)                       → drives
  useSpeedProfile  → DrivingRepository.speedProfile(vehicleId, start, end)
                       (GET /analytics/speed-profile [start, end])             → speedProfileState

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  The analytics payload + the drives stay SI end to end (m/s, Wh, meters). Display conversion
  happens only at the render boundary via SpeedProfileDisplayPrefs.toSpeed/toEfficiency
  (convertSpeedFromSI from the shared units module + the Wh/km→Wh/mi 1.609344 factor). The hero
  gauges convert avg/peak/optimal m/s; the bucket-label boundaries are compared against the
  converted display speed exactly as the web does (the mph-derived labels are upstream-owned).

